.DS_Store
__pycache__/
ONLINE_SETUP.md
DESIGN_REPORT.md
notes/
node_modules/

# art-review/ is deliberately NOT ignored, despite what
# .planning/art-generation-process.md §6 says. Gemini output is not reproducible —
# the same prompt gives a different image — so the repo is the only backup of
# art that cannot be remade, and ignored files are one `git clean -xdf` from
# gone. Revisit when the tracked total passes ~700 MB (Pages caps a published
# site at 1 GB): at that point move the whole folder to an orphan
# `art-archive` branch rather than ignoring it.

# hook scratch: per-session markers for read-the-doc-first
.claude/hooks/.read-state/

# stage_layout_check.mjs writes its contact sheet + screenshots here on every run —
# 142MB of transient probe output per pass; evidence lives in the gate's log and
# the commit messages, never in the repo
layout-check-shots/

# Sea-trial / probe output — thousands of PNGs per run, regenerated on every trial.
# Added 2026-08-26 after `git add -A` staged 15,913 of them into the cutover commit.
sea-trial-shots/
crew-phone-shots/
seed-drill-shots/
mp-rig-shots/
playtest-gate/

# Chrome/Chromium profiles from playtest runs. NEVER commit a --user-data-dir.
# On 2026-08-26, commit 5d82213 added 15 of these (10,713 files, 142 MB) because a
# playtest pointed --user-data-dir INSIDE the repo instead of /tmp. GitHub's secret
# scanner then fired on Default/shared_proto_db/000003.log — it had found the Google
# API key that is baked into every copy of Chrome, sent as X-Goog-Api-Key to
# optimizationguide-pa.googleapis.com. That key is Google's, not ours, so there was
# nothing to rotate; the cost was 142 MB in a public repo and a 3:50am alert email.
# A profile also carries Cookies, Login Data and History — these were empty because
# the profiles were freshly made, which is luck, not a guarantee. See
# docs/DRIVING-THE-GAME.md §8a: user-data-dir belongs in /tmp.
#
# The globs must cover EVERY name the QA scripts give a profile, not just the one
# that leaked. Checked against 4/scripts on main 2026-08-26: playtest_gate.mjs makes
# prof-<name>-a and prof-sheet-<tag> (these are the ones that leaked), group_g_peek_probe
# prof, group_f/g_shots prof-<TAG>, mp_rig prof-host and prof-guest, mouse_qa profile,
# stage_layout_check profile-<W>x<H>, contact_sheet _sheet-profile. A name-by-name list
# rots the moment someone adds a script, so these are deliberately shape-based.
# Note playtest_gate.mjs defaults --out to ./playtest-gate (inside the repo), so the
# default run is caught here too, not only the --out that caused the incident.
prof/
prof-*/
profile/
profile-*/
_sheet-profile/
chrome-probe*/
.pw-profile-*/

# Two more scripts still default their --out INSIDE the repo: mouse_qa.mjs
# (./mouse-qa-shots) and narration_timeline.mjs (./narration-timeline). The profile
# globs above already catch the profile each one creates; these two lines cover the
# screenshots beside it, which are the same transient probe output as every other
# directory in this block. Added in the same commit as the globs rather than waiting
# for a third incident to make the case.
mouse-qa-shots/
narration-timeline/

# The CTO lock: written when a marathon worker starts, removed when it stops. Machine-local
# state, never history — and .claude/hooks/cto-staging-only.cjs keys the main-branch block on it.
.planning/.cto-lock

# ANY *-shots/ directory is transient probe output — the list above was hand-kept and rotted
# (w1-smoke-shots/ appeared 2026-08-28 and was not on it). The glob is the derived answer.
*-shots/
w1-crewphone-recheck/
# ^ named outside the -shots convention and paid for it immediately: name probe output dirs *-shots so the glob above covers them without this file growing a list again.

# wyclau machine-local files (the Bell and the Glass generator read/write these). Per-machine
# by nature: each one's answer is only true about itself. The CROSS-MACHINE view is the tracked
# .planning/wyclau/status/<hostname>.md, published by scripts/wyclau/publish_status.mjs — never
# these originals. (Several names below belong to the pre-2026-09-01 watchdog and are kept so a
# straggler machine that still writes them cannot dirty the tree.)
.planning/wyclau/HEARTBEAT
.planning/wyclau/glass.html
.planning/wyclau/restarts.log
.planning/wyclau/LAST-LAUNCH
.planning/wyclau/LAST-ACTIVITY
.planning/wyclau/LAST-PUBLISH
.planning/wyclau/STOP-HOOK-STATE.json
# Written by a long job (a sea trial) as it progresses; read by the Glass for the status dot.
# Per-machine by nature and actively misleading if shared: committed, it would describe a job
# running on somebody else's computer.
.planning/wyclau/LONG-RUN
# Detached-trial stdout/stderr logs (start_trial_detached.mjs) — bulky, machine-local.
.planning/wyclau/detached/

# Claude Code local settings are MACHINE-LOCAL by design (the file even points at
# /opt/homebrew). It was tracked once and shipped the Mac's 82-entry approval history
# to every clone; the deliberate, reviewed allowlist lives in .claude/settings.json.
.claude/settings.local.json
.planning/wyclau/LAST-HARVEST

# A rung watch's stdout/stderr (bell.ps1). Machine-local and often large; the DURABLE record of
# what a watch did is its own commits and .planning/wyclau/status/<hostname>.md.
.planning/wyclau/watch-*.out
.planning/wyclau/watch-*.err

# Scratch from the asset-compression tools (scripts/qa/asset_*.mjs, boot_weight_probe.mjs):
# candidate art, a copy of assets/ taken while posing a before/after pair, screenshots, and the
# Chrome profiles those probes launch. All regenerable, all bulky — .tmp-after-assets alone is a
# second copy of the whole art tree. Shape-based rather than a list, for the same reason the
# profile globs above are: a hand-kept list rots the moment someone adds a script.
.tmp-*/
# ...and the loose FILES those same probes drop beside them — `.tmp-dispsize-modal-phone.png` and
# friends. The directory glob above did not cover a file, so three screenshots sat untracked at the
# repo root next to index.html until CEO 83 counted them. Same shape, same reason.
.tmp-*
